.SS "GtkWidget* icon_get_by_file (const char * text, const char * file, const char * mime)"
.PP
create a GTK-'icon' for a file, by thumbnailing it, or by finding an image for its MIME-type. 
.PP
called from \fBbrowser_view::browser_view_dir()\fP to create column-icons. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fItext\fP - the text for the icon's label 
.br
\fIfile\fP - the file the icon stands for 
.br
\fImime\fP - the file's MIME-type
.RE
.PP

.SS "static GtkWidget* icon_get_by_path (const char * text, const char * ip)\fC [static]\fP"
.PP
create a GTK-'icon' for a file. 
.PP
called from \fBbrowser_view::browser_view_dir()\fP to create column-icons. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fItext\fP - the text for the icon's label 
.br
\fIip\fP - the file containing the image-data for the icon
.RE
.PP

.SS "GtkWidget* icon_get_by_path_no_resize (const char * ip)"
.PP
create a GTK-'icon' from an image. 
.PP
most basic procedure -- no labels, conversions, searching, or resizing. called from \fBabout::about_init()\fP. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIip\fP - icon-path
.RE
.PP

.SS "int icon_init (void)"
.PP
initialize icon sub-system. 
.PP
tries to find a picture of the user for her home-directory.
.SS "GdkPixbuf* pixbuf_get_by_path_and_resize (const char * ip, int size, int interpolate)"
.PP
create a GDK pixbuf from an image and resize it if necessary. 
.PP
called by various in icon-view, tooltip, shelf, actions. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIip\fP - icon-path 
.br
\fIsize\fP - if image exceeds box of size*size, scale it to fit (retain aspect) 
.br
\fIinterpolate\fP - quality: GDK_INTERP_BILINEAR or GDK_INTERP_HYPER
.RE
.PP

